   "id": 512804,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The height in feet, <span data-math=\"h\">h</span>, of an object shot upwards into the air with initial velocity, <span data-math=\"{v_0}\">{v_0}</span>, after <span data-math=\"t\">t</span> seconds is given by the formula <span data-math=\"h = - 16{t^2} + {v_0}t\">h = - 16{t^2} + {v_0}t</span>. A firework is shot upwards with initial velocity 130 feet per second. How many seconds will it take to reach a height of 260 feet? Round to the nearest tenth of a second.",
